Definition 3 (Conditional probability mass function) Let \(X\) and \(Y\) be jointly distributed discrete random variables. The conditional probability mass function of \(Y\) given \(X = x\) (for values of \(x\) with \(\operatorname{P}(X = x) &gt; 0\)) is:
\[\operatorname{P}(Y = y \mid X = x) \stackrel{\text{def}}{=}\frac{\operatorname{P}(X = x,\, Y = y)}{\operatorname{P}(X = x)}\]











